(1)+(2) the lonely point t* sits in a mult-of-14 BACKBONE gap; which runners BIND there:
family                     | M | t* | backbone (mult14) | binding runners at t* (dist=M)
single-killer {1..12,182}  |  14/183 |  14/183 | [182] | [1, 182]   (backbone lonely@t*: True)
ladder S_2 {1..12,364}     |  28/365 |  28/365 | [364] | [1, 364]   (backbone lonely@t*: True)
multi-killer {1..11,13,84} |    7/89 |   37/89 | [84] | [5, 84]   (backbone lonely@t*: True)
multi {1..10,13,22,84}     |    2/23 |    2/23 | [84] | [1, 22]   (backbone lonely@t*: True)

=> single-killer: ONLY runner 1 + the backbone bind (=> the 2-runner balance, PROVED cont.60/61).
   multi-killer: MORE runners bind (the fillers engage) => the backbone gap is contested, mid-interval.

(3) the GRID-POINT modular covering law: near j/14, a runner b covers iff 14|bj iff b==0 mod 14/gcd(j,14):
     j | gcd(j,14) | need b == 0 mod | covered by
     1 |         1 |             14 | mult 14
     2 |         2 |              7 | mult 7
     3 |         1 |             14 | mult 14
     4 |         2 |              7 | mult 7
     5 |         1 |             14 | mult 14
     6 |         2 |              7 | mult 7
     7 |         7 |              2 | even (mult 2)
     8 |         2 |              7 | mult 7
     9 |         1 |             14 | mult 14
    10 |         2 |              7 | mult 7
    11 |         1 |             14 | mult 14
    12 |         2 |              7 | mult 7
    13 |         1 |             14 | mult 14
    => all 13 grid points are COVERED by any covering family (has mult 14 -> covers the 6 coprime-14
       points and (14=2*7) the 6 even + the j=7 point). So gaps are strictly BETWEEN grid points,
       inside the backbone's inter-arc slots -- the covering-min lives in one backbone gap.
